@startuml
title RTSyn v1.0.0 - Functional flow

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor User
participant "GUI or CLI\nclient" as Client
participant "HTTP API\nserver thread" as Api
queue "Command SPSC" as Commands
participant "Engine\nRT cycle thread" as Engine
participant "Runtime + ABI nodes" as Runtime
queue "Result SPSC" as Results
queue "Telemetry SPSC\nevents + values" as TelemetryQueue
participant "Telemetry drain\nnon-RT thread" as Drain
database "JSONL values\noptional CSV" as Files

== Start and control ==
User -> Client: Launch GUI or CLI
Client -> Api: HTTP request
Api -> Commands: enqueue command
Engine -> Commands: consume at a cycle boundary
Engine -> Runtime: apply graph, node, or timing change
Engine -> Results: publish result when required
Results --> Api: correlated result
Api --> Client: HTTP response

== Realtime cycle ==
loop Every configured period
    Engine -> Runtime: step()
    activate Runtime
    Runtime -> Runtime: device immediate/read
    Runtime -> Runtime: propagate current-cycle connections
    Runtime -> Runtime: plugin processing
    Runtime -> Runtime: propagate current-cycle connections
    Runtime -> Runtime: device terminal/write
    Runtime -> Runtime: stage cyclic plugin edges for next cycle
    Runtime --> Engine: stage timestamps
    deactivate Runtime
    Engine -> TelemetryQueue: events, measurements, subscribed values
    Engine -> Engine: sleep until absolute deadline
end

== Non-RT telemetry ==
Drain -> TelemetryQueue: drain events and values
Drain -> Files: append JSONL / CSV
Client -> Api: query nodes, status, measurements
Api --> Client: cached non-RT snapshot
Client -> Files: GUI tails JSONL values when needed

note over Runtime
Device-to-plugin and plugin-to-device data propagate in the same cycle.
Only cyclic plugin-to-plugin dependencies advance by one cycle.
end note

== Stop ==
User -> Client: Stop daemon
Client -> Api: global stop request
Api -> Commands: enqueue stop
Engine -> Engine: leave RT loop

@enduml
